# HP39gs stock launch through the original APLET UI and serial disk.
# The stock ROM mounts the host directory over Kermit, reads HP39DIR.*, then
# lazily fetches the selected aplet and library when ENTER launches it.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6

# HP39 matrix aliases:
#   G/H/I -> SYMB/PLOT/NUM
#   J/K/L -> HOME/APLET/VIEWS
7000 tap aplet
8000 capture aplet-library
9000 tap f5
10000 capture receive-menu

# HP39/40 2.22 RECEIVE FROM order:
#   HP39 (IrDA), HP39/40 (USB), HP39/40 (Ser),
#   USB Disk drive, Ser. Disk drive.
10500 tap down
11200 tap down
11900 tap down
12600 tap down
12900 capture receive-serial-disk
13300 tap enter

# HP39DIR.CUR and HP39DIR.000 complete first; ENTER then lazily installs the
# selected aplet and Library 275. ENTER does not cancel an in-progress transfer
# (ON does), so retry periodically instead of guessing exact completion time.
31000 capture remote-aplet
32500 tap enter
34000 capture lazy-fetch
180000 tap enter
190000 tap enter
200000 tap enter
210000 tap enter
220000 tap enter
230000 tap enter
240000 tap enter
250000 tap enter
260000 tap enter
270000 tap enter
280000 tap enter

# Current x50ng evidence shows HP39gs can still be actively transferring the
# 42,022-byte HPGCC000.000 at the old ~295 s deadline, while the sibling HP40gs
# path has completed its larger lazy-fetch chain by roughly 371 s. Keep the
# same bounded sparse tail as HP40gs so active Kermit progress is not classified
# as a launcher timeout, while leaving wide gaps after a successful ENTER launch.
310000 tap enter
340000 tap enter
370000 tap enter
400000 tap enter
34500 monitor 390000
